<task id="230" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Repo-deployed system playbooks are read-only in the BFF: canvas save, JIT sync and the per-node routes refuse to change them (#1698, #1498)</title>
    <phase>13 Deferred-issue triage group C (R1 close-out)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF code (.cs).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Guards destructive writes on deployed AI playbooks; a wrong rule either keeps the wipe hazard or locks user-authored playbooks.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>group-c-2026-11-26a</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Services/Ai NodeService / PlaybookEndpoints / NodeEndpoints and AnalysisOrchestrationService JIT sync; no Signals files.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-26: "Yes, start group C" (deferred-issue triage group C, notes/deferred-triage-2026-11.md). Read gh issue view 1698 and gh issue view 1498 (with its pickup comment). NodeService.SyncCanvasToNodesAsync (Services/Ai/NodeService.cs ~381; callers PlaybookEndpoints.cs ~728 PUT canvas, AnalysisOrchestrationService.cs ~204 JIT sync) deletes every node without a __canvasNodeId marker and recreates stubs, so one Designer save of a deployed system playbook wipes it. PR #1497 (branch fix/designer-readonly-system-playbooks, still open, far behind master) adds NodeService.EnsureCanvasSyncAllowedAsync (protected = sprk_issystemplaybook true OR sprk_playbooktype = 2 OR any node lacks the marker; fail closed: unreadable = refuse; PUT canvas 409 playbook_read_only / 503 playbook_canvas_unverifiable before persisting; JIT logs and runs on stored nodes) with 14 tests. Bring that change onto a fresh branch from origin/master (cherry-pick or re-apply; do not merge the stale branch), then apply the same guard to the per-node routes in Api/Ai/NodeEndpoints.cs (create, update, delete, scopes) returning 409 with zero writes, and make per-node writes on user playbooks not trip the unmarked-node rule (stamp the marker or exempt them). First search scripts/ and src/client for callers of the per-node routes on system playbooks; if deploy tooling uses them, STOP (escalation). The main session closes PR #1497 with a pointer after the new PR merges. Line numbers at origin/master d43fc9e16d.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, the AI playbook node model.</role>
  <goal>No BFF path (canvas save, JIT sync, per-node create/update/delete/scopes) can change a repo-deployed system playbook's nodes, while user-authored playbooks keep working.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Project CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha (2026-10-09): never open and save a system playbook in the Designer; this task is what lets that gotcha relax later (the main session edits CLAUDE.md, not you). Live check from the issue: every playbook with unmarked nodes on dev is a system/notification playbook. ADR-013: AI via PublicContracts; keep new types inside Services/Ai.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (Signals code: "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes the contract baselines; Communication: "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"; Ai: "FullyQualifiedName~Ai"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene when the BFF changes: publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface, endpoint or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests (build tests/Spaarke.ArchTests explicitly first). Client code: run node scripts/quality/client-lint/client-lint.mjs check and the package jest suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses, tenant names or private access-control mechanics in code, tests, notes, commits or the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §2 / D-106">Fix only what the named issues describe. Any other defect found: report it in the task notes and to the main session; do not fix it here.</constraint>
  </constraints>
